{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101788","id":2286066195,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6IQpoT","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101788","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101788.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101788.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101788","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101788/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101788/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101788/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/b7566b9848dce0b808f490c43f19d77038444e83","number":101788,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Add `use_self_delta_to_fade` to NodeOneShot to fade finished animation","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"- Fixes https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101169\r\n\r\nFirst, note that this is a band-aid solution.\r\n\r\nFor example, when there is a 1 second fade in OneShot, when the input TimeScale is 2.0, the fade is actually 0.5 seconds.\r\n\r\nThis is a fix to address the problem noted in #87009 and to keep the past behavior that has existed since 3.x, but I assume it is not correct in terms of consistency.\r\n\r\nFor complete consistency, I think the NodeTimeInfo should include the TimeScale and get the remaining time depending on that. However, this is a major rework and should not be done at this stage as it would be a significant behavior change. So, I believe we should rethink this when the update timing to 5.0. (So this and https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101792 using prediction.)\r\n\r\nFor now, enabling this option will allow the fade to work even when the input animation delta is `0`.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNzkwOTY5OTc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/archived","name":"archived","description":"","color":"aaaaaa","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":2666705648,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwyNjY2NzA1NjQ4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:animation","name":"topic:animation","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2025-01-19T06:20:49Z","updated_at":"2026-06-26T16:48:41Z","closed_at":"2025-05-17T22:45:53Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5b17eb21fbfcedb32be1fd527398113b2fd71daa","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"TokageItLab:fix-oneshot-delta","ref":"fix-oneshot-delta"